{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Look down from Your holy habitation.</b> We have done what You decreed upon us; do You what You promised us. <br><b>And bless Your people.</b> With sons and daughters. <br><b>And the land that You gave us.</b> With rains of favor, blessing, and freewill-offering. <br><b>As You swore to our fathers, a land flowing with milk and honey.</b> That You give flavor in the fruits. And elsewhere they interpreted: השקיפה ממעון קדשך — we have done what is incumbent upon us to do; do You what is incumbent upon You. And the reason he mentioned מעון קדשך and did not say מכון, as Solomon said in his prayer (I Kings 8:39): ״ואתה תשמע השמים מכון שבתך״, is because the confession that one rejoices in upon completing his obligation in the separation of his terumot and ma'asrot — that rejoicing is in His מעון, that is, in that firmament whose name is מעון; therefore he mentioned מעון קדשך. And the reason he used the language of השקיפה, which is never mentioned anywhere except in punishment, is to show how great is the reward of mitzvot when performed with joy, for joy transforms the attribute of judgment into the attribute of mercy. And so our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted: Rabbi Chanina bar Pappa said: Come and see how great is the power of gifts to the poor — every השקיפה in the Torah is for ill, but here it is for blessing." "<b>And if</b> you gain insight into the matter of these gifts in their mystical secret, you will find that the terumah called ראשית alludes to חכמה, which embraces בינה in fifty gates, and therefore the Torah is one of fifty; this is what they said: תרומה — תרי ממאה (two out of a hundred). And the first tithe given to the Levite, who was tenth among the sons, corresponds to the tenth part; and likewise the second tithe also corresponds to the tenth part, for the first tithe is so called because it is first for us, and the second tithe is likewise so called because it is tenth to the first supreme one. And the poor man's tithe, which one separates in the third and sixth years, corresponds to the sefirah of יסוד, which is the balancing one, and is included within the seven; so too the separation of the poor man's tithe came in the middle of six years — three from here and three from here — and with this tithe all the tithes were completed, both above and below. This is what it says: כי תכלה לעשר את כל מעשר תבואתך בשנה השלישית — it says כי תכלה, for this poor man's tithe is the culmination and end of all the tithes. And therefore Scripture said in the parashah of Re'eh, in the section of עשר תעשר (Deuteronomy 14:28): מקצה שלש שנים תוציא את כל מעשר תבואתך בשנה ההיא והנחת בשעריך — for just as the Holy One, blessed be He, commanded that we gather all the tithes of the past years in one place, in our gates, so too the allusion herein is that we gather and unify everything without division in the place that encompasses all — this is what it says: והנחת בשעריך, which is the gate of prayer; it is the gate of HaShem that encompasses all. And therefore he would pray in the holy tongue, and would confess in a loud voice that he had completed his obligation in his tithes of the Holy One, blessed be He, and had separated them in the proper order and proper intention, and did not alter the order, heaven forbid. This is the meaning of ככל מצותך אשר צויתני — rather, he ordered everything in his thought and unified everything in complete unity. לא עברתי — I did not cut down the plantings; ולא שכחתי — I did not forget to bless HaShem and the Kingship, for that is the complete unity. And he further confesses and says: לא אכלתי באוני ממנו — I did not separate it for any force among the forces of the angels, which are ten gradations that are near to Him; nor for any force among the forces of the spheres. ולא בערתי ממנו בטמא — it goes without saying that I did not separate from it for any force among the forces of spiritual impurity that dwell below, in the air between the spheres and the elements. ולא נתתי ממנו למת — it goes without saying that I did not separate it for any one of the four elements, which are dead bodies and not spiritual. But שמעתי בקול ה' — to the Name, the unique Name alone, which is supreme over all of them, ועשיתי ככל אשר צויתני. השקיפה ממעון קדשך — this prayer is directed to the glorious Name, for so it says: ואמרת לפני ה' אלהיך, and to Him he says השקיפה. And he says ממעון, for הוד והדר לפניו, and rivers of rejoicing and rivers of joy, and the joy is in His מעון. This is השקיפה ממעון קדשך — he says: Look down upon us from Your holy habitation and pour out upon us what You have received from heaven, as in (I Kings 8:32) ״ואתה תשמע השמים״. Or one may say: Cause our prayer to be heard to heaven, וברך את עמך את ישראל — bestow upon them the blessing that You have received. And this is the language of our Sages, of blessed memory: we have done what is incumbent upon us; do You what is incumbent upon You. ואת האדמה — corresponding to it is the supernal land, which is ארץ זבת חלב ודבש, which is the will that pours forth mercy and judgment; this is the meaning of ארץ זבת חלב ודבש, and I have already mentioned this. And everything is true, both above and below, and this is clear."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:51:34.837103962Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}